# The 3D view (domains/visualization). The engine draws a scene, and a source fills it in: the
# simulator, or the telemetry of a real plane. This section is about the second source. The
# tests run with no window: MAVLink in, the scene out. See
# domains/visualization/telemetry/tests/acceptance.rs.

Section: Watching a real plane
  The 3D view of the simulator can also show a real plane. `sim001_view` listens for the
  [[MAVLink]] telemetry of the plane, and it puts the plane in the same scenery as the
  simulator. It does not fly anything. You can watch a flight from the pilot box, from behind
  the plane or from its nose, and a camera system can learn from the same pictures.

  The view puts [[home]] at the pilot box. Use a map pack of the field (`--map NAME`) when
  the scenery must match the real place.

Vocabulary:
  State: the telemetry is flowing | silent
    Set: let the telemetry of the plane be {value}
    Shows: flowing: the autopilot sends its attitude and its position a few times a second
  State: the reported distance north of home is 0..2000 m
    Set: fly the plane {value} north of home
  State: the reported height is 0..500 m
    Set: fly the plane at {value} above home
  State: the reported bank is 0..90 degrees
    Set: bank the plane {value} to the right
  State: the reported heading is north | east | south | west
    Set: turn the plane to fly {value}
  State: the plane in the view is missing | shown
    Shows: missing: the view shows the scenery and no plane
    Shows: shown: the view shows the plane
  State: the distance north of the pilot box in the view is 0..2000 m
    Shows: the plane in the view is {value} north of the pilot box
  State: the height above the pilot box in the view is 0..500 m
    Shows: the plane in the view is {value} above the ground at the pilot box
  State: the right wing in the view is low | level | high
    Shows: low: the plane in the view banks to the right
  State: the heading in the view is north | east | south | west
    Shows: the nose of the plane in the view points {value}

  Event: 1 second passes
    Say: wait 1 second
  Event: 10 seconds pass
    Say: wait 10 seconds

  Phrase: the view is listening
    Say: start `sim001_view`. It listens for MAVLink on UDP port 14550
    Given the plane in the view is missing
    And the telemetry is silent
    And the reported distance north of home is 0 m
    And the reported height is 0 m
    And the reported bank is 0 degrees
    And the reported heading is north

Background:
  Follows: the launcher has just opened
  Given the view is listening
